            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic congestion syndrome: demonstration and diagnosis by helical CT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pelvic pain is a common gynaecological complaint, sometimes without any obvious etiology. We report a case of pelvic congestion syndrome, an often overlooked cause of pelvic pain, diagnosed by helical computed tomography. This seems to be an effective and noninvasive imaging modality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
